      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled dose.\n\n- **Maximum daily dose:** The FDA-labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day. For extended-release it's 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Maximum single dose:** Single doses are usually capped at 850\u20131,000 mg. 1,700 mg is well above that.\n- **Risk:** At this dose, lactic acidosis and GI toxicity are real concerns, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max for IR)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter that."
      }
